From e5b55dd6dfb3d3ccf26a0d075d3ed30b034ca52f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fan Kai <fankai@onero.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 17:25:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Meter Pro CO2 not discoverable via BT proxies

- Add METER_PRO_C back to NON_CONNECTABLE_SUPPORTED_MODEL_TYPES while
  keeping it in CONNECTABLE_SUPPORTED_MODEL_TYPES.
- Update config_flow to allow auto-discovery from non-connectable sources
  for devices that support both connectable and non-connectable operation.
- Update async_setup_entry to use non-connectable BLE lookup for
  dual-mode devices so setup succeeds via passive BT proxies.
- Add complete tests for Meter Pro CO2 discovery from non-connectable source.

PR #163008 moved METER_PRO_C to connectable-only, which broke discovery
and setup via passive BT proxies (Shelly/ESPHome).

Fixes #164817

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
